From: PowerVLC <powervlc@localhost>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fill the logical SPU stream number in the stream change event

dvdnav_spu_stream_change_event_t documents a "logical" member as "The
logical (DVD) stream number", and the audio counterpart fills its own,
but the subpicture event leaves it uninitialised: callers read whatever
was in the buffer.

That member is the only way for a caller to tell "the disc selected
subpicture stream N" apart from "the disc selected no subpicture at
all".  vm_get_subp_active_stream() cannot express the difference: when
SPST_REG holds no valid selection -- which is the case right after
vm_reset(), where it is set to 62 -- the lookup fails and the function
silently falls back to the first available stream, then flags it hidden
because the register carries no display bit.  A player then believes the
disc asked for "stream 0, forced subtitles only" and selects that track.

position_next.spu_channel already carries SPST_REG verbatim (see
vm_get_position() in vm/vm.c), so publishing it costs one assignment:
values 0-31 are a real selection, bit 0x40 is the display flag, and
anything above is "no subpicture selected".

--- a/src/dvdnav.c
+++ b/src/dvdnav.c
@@ -797,6 +797,7 @@
     (*len) = sizeof(dvdnav_spu_stream_change_event_t);
     stream_change->physical_wide      = vm_get_subp_active_stream(this->vm, 0);
     stream_change->physical_letterbox = vm_get_subp_active_stream(this->vm, 1);
     stream_change->physical_pan_scan  = vm_get_subp_active_stream(this->vm, 2);
+    stream_change->logical            = this->position_next.spu_channel;
     this->position_current.spu_channel = this->position_next.spu_channel;
 #ifdef LOG_DEBUG
     Log3(this, "SPU_STREAM_CHANGE stream_id_wide=%d",stream_change->physical_wide);
